  "Description": "feature.chamfer on one edge at a time: a horizontal (oneTop) and a vertical (oneVertical) convex edge of a 40x30x20 box with distance 4, the same top edge unsymmetric with 4 on the top face ('primaryFace') and 2 on the front face (asymmetric), the circular top rim of a cylinder (cylRim, a conical chamfer) and the concave vertical edge of an L shaped prism (lConcave, adds material). asymmetricFront chamfers the same edge with the roles of the faces swapped: 4 on the front face ('primaryFace'), 2 on the top face.",
  "Expected": "Closed forms. oneTop: 24000 - 8*40 = 23680. oneVertical: 24000 - 8*20 = 23840. asymmetric: 24000 - 4*2/2*40 = 23840; the top face must end at y=4 and the front face at z=18, so the chamfer face runs from (y=0, z=18) to (y=4, z=20). Volume, area and extent are the same with swapped distances, so asymmetricSlice intersects the result with the slab y <= 3: right 2400 - 40 * integral_0^3 (2 - y/2) dy = 2400 - 150 = 2250, swapped 2400 - 40 * integral_0^2 (4 - 2y) dy = 2240. cylRim: R=10, h=20, d=2, the triangle 2*2/2 revolved at the radius 10 - 2/3: 2000 pi - 2 pi (28/3) 2 = 5888/3 pi = 6165.899181, surfaces 2 planes + cylinder + cone. lConcave: 12000 + 8*20 = 12160. asymmetricFront: same volume 23840, but the chamfer face runs from (y=0, z=16) to (y=2, z=20), so asymmetricFrontSlice = 2240. The two slices differ only if 'primaryFace' is honoured: with the distances bound to the edge's own PrimaryFace one of the two slices is wrong.",
